This code provides a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B that continuously samples the analog voltage from a Honeywell AWM720P airflow sensor using an MCP3008 ADC connected on SPI channel 0 with chip-enable 0 at a 1 MHz clock. It triggers a sample every 100 ms, converts each voltage to airflow using the provided calibration curve, and appends each reading together with a timestamp to a file named `airflow_log.txt`. The program handles ADC read errors gracefully, includes robust error handling for all initialization steps, and runs indefinitely until interrupted. It catches SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to close the SPI handle, close the log file, terminate the driver library, and release all resources on any exit path.

