This code sets up a Raspberry Pi to control four relays connected to GPIO pins 17, 22, 23, and 24. It uses the `libgpiod` library to manage the GPIO pins. The program initializes the GPIO lines, sets them to low (inactive), and then enters an infinite loop where it sequentially activates each relay for one second, deactivates it, and waits one second before moving to the next relay. The program handles signals to ensure that all relays are deactivated and resources are released when the program is terminated.

