This code sets up two TCRT5000 IR reflective sensors on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the `libgpiod` library. It logs the binary readings from the sensors along with timestamps to a file named `obstacle_log.txt` every 100 milliseconds. The program includes robust error handling for GPIO setup failures, handles sensor read failures by logging errors to `stderr`, and performs a graceful shutdown on `SIGINT` (Ctrl+C) by releasing all resources before exiting.

