This code implements a PID-controlled greenhouse heater using a DS18B20 temperature sensor, a relay, and hardware PWM on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the temperature, computes the PID output, sets the PWM duty cycle and relay state, and logs the data every 5 seconds. The program handles errors and cleans up resources on exit.

