```

This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to sample a BMP180 pressure sensor on I2C bus 1 every 50 ms, storing the readings in a circular buffer. It calculates a rolling average of the pressure readings and asserts an active-HIGH alert on GPIO24 if the current pressure deviates by more than 5 hPa from the average. The program handles I2C failures, sensor absence, and exits cleanly on SIGINT.

