This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to interface with two Sensirion SLF3S-1300F liquid flow sensors using I2C bus 1. It uses a Sensirion SF06 multiplexer breakout or a comparable I2C hub to select between the sensors. The program reads three bytes from each sensor (two data bytes followed by a CRC-8 byte), validates the checksum, and retries up to three times on any I2C error before giving up. Valid readings are logged to `flow_log.txt` in the specified format. The program handles clean shutdown on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by closing all I2C handles and terminating the driver library.

