This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to interface with an OPT3001 ambient light sensor over I2C. It configures the sensor for continuous conversion with automatic full-scale range, reads the lux values, and appends them to a file with an ISO-8601 timestamp. The program handles I2C transaction failures and sensor-absent conditions by retrying or logging errors. It also performs a clean shutdown on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by releasing resources.

