This code sets up a Raspberry Pi to read RPM from a Melexis MLX90217 Hall-effect sensor using the `libgpiod` library. It configures the GPIO pin as an input with an internal pull-up resistor, counts rising-edge pulses using GPIO interrupts, and logs the RPM to a file and stdout every second. The program handles errors and exits gracefully on signals.

