This code sets up a Raspberry Pi to monitor two Hall-Effect sensors connected to GPIO pins 17 and 18. It logs the sensor states to a CSV file and calculates the RPM based on rising edges detected by the sensors. The program handles errors gracefully, including GPIO initialization failures and file I/O errors, and ensures that all resources are released properly on exit. It also handles SIGINT to perform orderly cleanup.

