This code sets up a Raspberry Pi to read data from an OPT3001 ambient light sensor using the I2C bus. It configures the sensor, reads the light data every second, and logs the data to a file and prints it to the console. The program handles errors gracefully, cleans up resources on exit, and swaps byte order as required by the sensor's data format.

