This code reads acceleration data from an Omron D7S-0001 vibration sensor over the I2C bus on a Raspberry Pi 5. It samples the X, Y, and Z axes every 100 ms and appends each sample to a file named `vibration_log.csv` with a header line "Timestamp,X,Y,Z". The program handles errors gracefully, detects the sensor-absent condition, and installs a SIGINT handler to cleanly close the I2C file descriptor and the CSV file on exit.

