This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to control two DC motors using a DRV8833 H-bridge with PWM and direction signals. It uses quadrature encoders to measure the motor speed and implements a PI control loop to maintain a target RPM. The program handles encoder stall detection, prints motor RPM and PWM duty cycle, and exits cleanly on SIGINT.

